      <Comment>|FRAME: 1-4-alpha-D-galacturonosyl &quot;Homogalacturonan&quot;| is a polysaccharide consisting of &amp;alpha;-1,4-linked |FRAME: D-GALACTURONATE| units. It is found in a highly methyl-esterified form when exported into cell walls. |FRAME: 1-4-alpha-D-galacturonosyl &quot;Homogalacturonan&quot;| forms one type of the backbones found in |FRAME: Pectin &quot;pectin&quot;|.</Comment>
